WEBVTT

00:25:29.484 --> 00:25:31.461
HW: So beautiful. So many more questions.

00:25:31.485 --> 00:25:32.635
I will be back.

00:25:33.389 --> 00:25:35.205
EG: Thanks, Helen.
CA: Thank you, Liz.

00:25:35.229 --> 00:25:37.557
I think the author's name
was Kate Braestrup.

00:25:37.581 --> 00:25:38.962
EG: That's it.

00:25:38.986 --> 00:25:41.607
CA: I guess that's a book,
if you need a book right now,

00:25:41.631 --> 00:25:43.541
"Here If You Need Me" by Kate Braestrup.

00:25:43.565 --> 00:25:44.715
EG: Very good, yeah.

00:25:45.198 --> 00:25:47.389
CA: Liz, you and I got to have
a conversation

00:25:47.413 --> 00:25:50.191
a few months after Rayya passed away.

00:25:50.215 --> 00:25:54.714
It was actually the first-ever episode
of the TED Interview podcast we did.

00:25:54.738 --> 00:25:59.723
And I found that it was probably
my favorite episode ever

00:25:59.747 --> 00:26:01.059
of the TED Interview.